---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Site
  title="Rathkit: built from scratch. Ships with nothing else."
  description="Rathkit builds libraries and tools with no runtime dependencies: RTE, a rich text editor, and Pack, a bundler written in Rust. Open source, with paid premium options for RTE."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Rathkit · RTE and Pack in development</p>
    <h1>Built from scratch.<br />Ships with nothing else.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Rathkit builds libraries and tools with no runtime dependencies. So far there is
      RTE, a rich text editor with first-party wrappers for the major frameworks, and
      Pack, a JavaScript and TypeScript bundler written in Rust. Open source, with paid
      premium options for RTE.
    </p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
      <a class="btn o" href="https://github.com/rathkit">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-h">
    <h2 id="proof-h" class="sr">What you install</h2>
    <pre class="code"><code><span class="dim">$</span> npm ls --omit=dev
<span class="dim">(empty)</span></code></pre>
    <p class="caption">Nothing in the box you didn't ask for.</p>
    <p class="note">
      This is the target for every Rathkit package. RTE is pre-release, so nothing is
      published yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="points" aria-label="Principles">
    <article>
      <h3>No runtime dependencies</h3>
      <p>
        Every package is written in-house. No dependency tree to audit, and nothing
        for an attacker to slip into between your lockfile and your users.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Pick only what you use</h3>
      <p>
        A small core, with features as separate plugin packages and thin wrappers for
        each framework. You ship only what you import.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Open source, paid premium</h3>
      <p>
        RTE's core and wrappers are open source. RTE's premium packages are delivered
        separately, with licenses that verify offline.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Site>

<style>
  .hero, .proof, .points { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding-inline: 16px; }
  .hero { padding-top: 56px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px; }
  .eyebrow { font: 500 0.75rem var(--rk-font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rk-brass-ink); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 4.4rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.02; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--rk-muted); max-width: 66ch; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .cta { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block; padding: 10px 18px; text-decoration: none;
    font: 700 0.9rem var(--rk-font-display);
    background: var(--rk-mark); color: var(--rk-on-mark); border: 1px solid var(--rk-mark);
  }
  .btn.o { background: transparent; color: var(--rk-fg); border-color: var(--rk-line); }
  .btn:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
  .proof { padding-top: 56px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
  .sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); }
  .code {
    margin: 0; background: var(--rk-sunk); border: 1px solid var(--rk-line);
    padding: 16px 18px; font: 0.95rem/1.6 var(--rk-font-mono); overflow-x: auto; max-width: 520px;
  }
  .dim { color: var(--rk-muted); }
  .caption { font: 700 1.2rem var(--rk-font-display); font-stretch: 112%; }
  .note { color: var(--rk-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; max-width: 72ch; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .points {
    padding-top: 72px; display: grid; gap: 16px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
  }
  .points article { background: var(--rk-surface); border: 1px solid var(--rk-line); padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .points p { color: var(--rk-muted); text-wrap: pretty; }
</style>
